  "description": "We took our classic long-haul bike and beefed up the braking so you can open it up on fast mountain roads. This steel frame touring bike is a nod to the past and looks perfectly in place cruising along Canada’s long, open highways. TRP Spyre C disc brakes keep you in control in all road and weather conditions. Shimano® components keep your ride rolling on long open stretches past the Saskatchewan-Manitoba border. It’s right around then that you’ll be thankful for the form-fitting comfort of the Brooks saddle, too.\n\nTriple-butted Reynolds 520 steel frame is solid and dependable\n\nTRP Spyre C disc brakes paired with 160mm rotors provide solid stopping power\n\nShimano Deore, LX and XT components provide granny-gear options for climbing in the Rockies and power gears for opening it up through the prairies\n\nTouring-ready wheels use 36 DT Swiss Champion spokes to lace the trusty Deore hubs to Mavic rims\n\n2 spares spokes are mounted to the non-driveside chainstay for when you really need them\n\n32mm Vittoria Randonneur Tech tires provides comfort, puncture resistance and grip on a wide variety of surfaces\n\nBrooks B17 for great comfort from one side of the province to the other\n\nRear disc mounts inside the rear triangle so it won’t interfere with racks or fenders\n\nBikes are covered by MEC's Rocksolid Guarantee and Bike Service Agreement. You can bring your bike to any MEC bike shop for free adjustments and minor maintenance for a year after purchase\n\nMEC bikes are designed in Canada. From frames, to graphics, to componentry builds, every element of the bike is developed at the MEC Head Office in Vancouver, BC",
